The normal to $bold(r) = bold(a) + lambda bold(u) + mu bold(v)$ is $bold(n) = bold(u) times bold(v)$, generally not a unit vector. The plane equation becomes $bold(r) dot bold(n) = k$ for a constant $k$, and the perpendicular distance from the origin to the plane is
$ hat(bold(n)) dot bold(r) = (k)/(abs(bold(n))). $
When three points $bold(a), bold(b), bold(c)$ lie in the plane, its equation is $(bold(r)-bold(a)) dot [(bold(b)-bold(a)) times (bold(c)-bold(a))] = 0$.
